{"name":"Treasure Island","hex":"#47493b","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"treasure","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A collection of valuable things; accumulated wealth; a stock of money, jewels, etc.","Anything greatly valued.\n\nA term of endearment.\n\n The female genitals; pudenda."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To consider to be precious; to value highly.","To store or stow in a safe place."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/treasure"},{"term":"island","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A contiguous area of land, smaller than a continent, totally surrounded by water.","A contiguous area of land, smaller than a continent, partially surrounded by water; a peninsula; a half-island."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To surround with water; make into an island.","To set, dot (as if) with islands."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/island"}],"entries":[{"title":"Treasure Island","blocks":[{"text":"Treasure Island is an adventure and historical novel by Scottish novelist Robert Louis Stevenson. It was published as a book in 1883, but is set in the 18th century, and tells a story of \"buccaneers and buried gold\". It is considered a coming-of-age story, and is noted for its atmosphere, characters, and action."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fe/Treasure_Island_%28title_page%2C_1883%29.webp/330px-Treasure_Island_%28title_page%2C_1883%29.webp?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Treasure_Island","wikidata":"Q185118"},{"title":"Treasure Island (TV franchise)","blocks":[{"text":"Treasure Island is a reality competition television franchise. The programme originated in New Zealand in 1997, where it was originally produced by Touchdown Television and broadcast by TVNZ, with later editions produced for broadcasters in Australia and Ireland. In the programme, contestants are isolated on a remote Fijian island and compete for a cash prize of NZ$25,000. From the 2019 edition, the winner of the Celebrity Treasure Island will receive NZ$100,000 and NZ$50,000 for the regular season their chosen charity."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Treasure_Island_(TV_franchise)","wikidata":"Q7836702"},{"title":"Treasure","blocks":[{"text":"Treasure is a concentration of wealth — often originating from ancient history — that is considered lost and/or forgotten until rediscovered. Some jurisdictions legally define what constitutes treasure, such as in the British Treasure Act 1996."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7a/Tesoro_de_Villena.jpg/330px-Tesoro_de_Villena.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Treasure","wikidata":"Q272937"},{"title":"Island","blocks":[{"text":"An island or isle is a piece of land, distinct from a continent, completely surrounded by water. There are continental islands, which were formed by being split from a continent by plate tectonics, and oceanic islands, which have never been part of a continent. Oceanic islands can be formed from volcanic activity, grow into atolls from coral reefs, and form from sediment along shorelines, creating barrier islands. River islands can also form from sediment and debris in rivers. Artificial islands are those made by humans, including small rocky outcroppings built out of lagoons and large-scale land reclamation projects used for development."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6b/Hawaje-NoRedLine.jpg/330px-Hawaje-NoRedLine.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Island","wikidata":"Q23442"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/06/Treasure-island01.png/500px-Treasure-island01.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://